     "story": "Forecasters' median bear (the supervisor did not restate scenarios): a real 2027-28 WFE downturn (customer capex cuts, AI-capex digestion, the Affiliates Rule returning after its extended suspension ends 2027-01-10); NTM EPS -20% (~$18.2) and the multiple -6 turns (16.5x). The supervisor's thesis break is $335 (~15x a ~$22.8 NTM EPS). Driver restatement: the -20% NTM EPS = WFE -15% vs path (2027-28 digestion), AGS -3% (Affiliates Rule returning: AMAT's 8-K of 2025-10-02 put the FY2026 net revenue effect at approximately $600 million, all segments, src 122), GM -1 pt; multiple -6 turns kept. Update 2026-11-04: the downside case also covers US data-center construction pauses spreading (Reuters/UBS 2026-11-05, src 53) and the Affiliates Rule returning when the suspension ends (BIS extended the Affiliates Rule suspension through 2027-01-10 (FR Doc. 2026-22793, filed for public inspection 2026-11-05, published and effective 2026-11-09; src 113, Nixon Peabody src 114)); deltas unchanged. Update 2026-11-05: the scenario-weighted data-center pause (Texas, PJM spread, Georgia, New York) is now in the base case through dc_mor x ai_wfe; the downside's WFE -15% stays the 2027-28 digestion and covers only a pause wider or longer than that weighted case, with no extra delta for it (not double-counted). Update 2026-11-13 (customer-capex build): the WFE -15% delta now applies to non-China foundry/logic capex, non-China memory capex and China Systems alike (cx_fl, cx_mem, ss_cn -15%), i.e. customers cut 2027-28 capex plans 15% against their stated budgets."
